{
    "attributes": {
        "action": "Commission a business case for UK sovereign data-centre network",
        "additional_details": "Public services need secure computing, storage & AI capacity. The Government should assess if public ownership could cut long-term costs, improve resilience, protect data and reduce reliance on technology companies. The business case should examine capital & operating costs, power & fibre availability, job creation, apprenticeship opportunities, cybersecurity, workloads, savings & income from leasing spare capacity. It should publish assumptions, shortlisted sites & recommendations.",
        "background": "Commission and publish an independent feasibility study and business case for building standardised modular data centres on suitable public land.\r\n\r\nIt should identify all potential sites and compare ten-year public ownership costs with continued reliance on commercial cloud and hosting providers.",
